## Purpose

Correct two field-exposed gaps where Tool Shed's convenience projections can disagree with
authoritative repository or execution truth: hard-coded release-tag formatting can select the
wrong cohort baseline, and stale campaign assignments can keep wholly terminal execution looking
active. Preserve completed PRM-0044 as historical delivery evidence; this is a focused follow-on
that makes release identity genuinely project-configurable and adds truthful terminal
administrative reconciliation.

## Desired Outcome

Repositories select a bounded declarative release-identity policy without modifying an installed
snapshot. Every release-cohort command shares one exact-tag-preserving, reachability-aware baseline
evaluator. Separately, campaigns with no runnable or nonterminal execution can use an explicit
guarded route that retires only proven stale assignments and closes into a distinct
administratively reconciled terminal result without claiming accepted-outcome success.

